https://github.com/markub3327/flappy-bird-gymnasium

main steps for implementing a Deep Q-Network (DQN) agent for the Flappy Bird environment. Here's the text version with short explanations:

0. Set Environment

Create and initialize the game environment where the agent will interact and learn.
Example: Flappy Bird Gymnasium environment.

1. Define DQN

Build a Deep Q-Network that takes the current state as input and predicts Q-values for all possible actions.
The network helps the agent decide which action is best in a given state.

2. Create Experience Replay

Store the agent's past experiences (state, action, reward, next_state, done) in a replay buffer.
Randomly sampling experiences improves training stability and reduces correlation between consecutive samples.

3. Multiple Episodes DQN Training Setup

Train the agent over many episodes so it can gradually learn better policies.
Each episode represents one complete game from start to termination.

4. Epsilon-Greedy Policy + Hyperparameters

Use an epsilon-greedy strategy to balance exploration and exploitation.
Important hyperparameters include learning rate, batch size, gamma (discount factor), and epsilon.

Epsilon Decay

Start with a high epsilon value (e.g., 1.0) to encourage exploration.
Gradually decrease epsilon (e.g., to 0.05) so the agent increasingly exploits learned knowledge.

7. Target Network

Maintain a separate target network whose weights are updated periodically from the main network.
This stabilizes learning by providing more consistent target Q-values.

8. Train & Test

Train the DQN agent using stored experiences and update network weights.
After training, test the agent without exploration to evaluate its performance.

Complete DQN Workflow
